J575d common TIPD/I2C split and ACE3 SPMI port against Linux
602042bf29f6efde39cfb5fdd9289bf4854bc0c5.

Semantically ports primary da16cc966d153550b2fc99e207ccc95cf32d5e31 and
550afd1aa62bb43183aad36aca4ba97580858dbe. Preserves the pinned core's
newer TPS66993 support, altmode/status layout and read_power_status callback.
The ACE3 data table wires that callback to the existing CD321x/TPS reader.
No older wholesale core replacement or speculative I2C ACE3 path is used.

Application: patch --batch --fuzz=0 -p0 from the pinned source root.
The four named child IRQs and board connector graph still require DT work.
This source port does not establish native power/IRQ/USB operation.

